{"metric":"kodama_kink","source":[{"metric":"kodama_kink","system":"areal","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"f4be9e7d115c9648"},{"metric":"kodama_kink","system":"proper_radial","fields":["coords","einstein_tensor","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"c97537e1dff05126"}],"views":[{"id":"proper_radial","label":"Proper radial distance","box":[-3.4916,3.4916,-3.3916,3.3916],"system":"proper_radial","settings":"$\\mu = 1$ and $f = 1.25$, so that the unit of every length is $1/\\mu$.","input":"Kodama's kink at $f = 1.25$, in units where $c = \\mu = 1$, solved from this spacetime's own $G^t{}_t$ and $G^\\theta{}_\\theta$ and the field's wave equation: a throat of areal radius $r_0 = 1.475/\\mu$, a mass $M$ on either side with $GM/c^2 = 0.390/\\mu$, and clocks at the throat running at $e^{h} = 0.703$ of the rate far away.","caption":["Kodama's kink at $f = 1.25$, each point in the diagram a 2-sphere of areal radius $r(R)$. Its metric functions $h$ and $r$ come from $G^t{}_t$, $G^\\theta{}_\\theta$, and the wave equation of the field, integrated numerically from the throat, and beyond the field's edge they are Schwarzschild's for the kink's mass on either side.","The tortoise coordinate $r_* = \\int e^{-h}\\,dR$ runs over the whole line, and $p, q = \\arctan((ct \\mp r_*)/r_0)$ bring the spacetime into the full diamond, with the throat on its axis and an $i^0$ and a pair of null infinities on each side. Light crosses the throat both ways, and no horizon stands anywhere."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416],[-3.1416,0.0],[0.0,-3.1416]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover","points":[[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416],[-3.1416,0.0],[0.0,-3.1416]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[0.0,-3.1409],[0.0028,-3.0678],[0.011,-2.9947],[0.0243,-2.922],[0.0434,-2.8464],[0.0671,-2.7717],[0.0965,-2.6939],[0.1724,-2.5285],[0.2852,-2.3259],[0.4327,-2.093